CONCEPT
  product:   Apogee
  one-liner: Aerospace-grade telemetry for the highest point of your life, which has already happened.
  premise:   a launch-services company that has quietly become an awards program. The peak is
             an apogee, achievements are burns, a class reunion is an atmospheric reentry event.
  demo:      Trajectory Console for one customer (Dale Renfro) — dossier rail, SVG flight path
             with hoverable burn markers, burn log with arm/safe toggle, reentry intercept list,
             and a launch-window control that only ever returns dates in the past.

DESIGN DIRECTION
  style:   Varsity trophy-case awards program, night-of-the-banquet dark mode. Felt panels on
           navy, 2px brass shelf rule as the only depth cue, chenille-patch shield motif for
           every awarded item, SVG apogee arc as the section rule.
  palette: primary #C8A548 (trophy brass) / accent #C4462F (descent red, quarantined to decline
           telemetry) / bg #12182B / fg #F2ECDC / muted #8E93A8 / ink #F2ECDC
  fonts:   display 'Anton' (banner caps), body 'Spectral' (awards-programme serif),
           telemetry 'IBM Plex Mono' (tabular figures)
  anti-sameness: checked against the last 7 entries (medium-for-doomscrollers, fortnite-for-
           divorced-dads, tesla-for-perpetual-interns, vercel-for-guys-named-steve,
           tesla-for-hedgehogs, instagram-for-plant-parents, lyft-for-ferrets). No collision on
           style, palette or font pairing. Nearest neighbours were the two dark entries
           (tesla-for-perpetual-interns aurora violet glass, tesla-for-hedgehogs slate
           automotive); this one is flat felt with no glass, no blur and no glow, on a warm
           brass carrier rather than a cool one.

